{"kind":"propose","text":"Amend the planner-added measurement form in overhead requestecbc722a criterion3. The user's target is10x less test overhead with useful invariants retained and heavy tests optimized. Establish that target for comparable complete-gate and normal edit-to-review workloads using elapsed pipeline/command time and aggregate process CPU (user+system over command descendants), with exact heads/commands/hardware/concurrency/cache/install conditions and honest reconstruction/shared-load limits. Summed component-command elapsed is an additional aggregate test-job measure and must say it is a sum, not an uninterrupted run. Any phase subtotal or serial suite-command comparison keeps its actual name and boundary. Remove the additional acceptance requirement to measure normal Vitest/Cloudflare pool-runner/process/isolate lifetimes or prove a cap-based lifetime bound: that demand came from the planner's unqualified aggregate-worker wording, not the user's instruction, and is not necessary to decide the requested pipeline-cost outcome. Do not call CPU, phases or serial command elapsed an observed worker lifetime. This explicitly changes that measurement requirement rather than pretending those quantities meet its former interpretation.\n\nThe whole10x outcome is not declared achieved by this decision. The checker still judges comparability and source correctness; include complete retained coverage, setup/compiler cost, no increased-parallelism-only or smoke/count claim, and a meaningful edit→affected checks→focused semantic controls→final compact complete gate. If either required comparable workload does not demonstrate10x on elapsed/process-cost evidence, record its bottleneck and continue reducing it. Keep all package/active acts/MCP test audits, compact invariant-to-witness map, useful actual authority/durability/retry/lease/transport/DO boundaries, heavy harness optimization, contributor guidance, exact final head and independent checker acceptance. The selector/no-test/timeout defects and truthful accounting labels remain to be corrected. No restored old suites, per-field quota, extra baseline, instrumentation framework, new lane, functional backlog closure or Jam gate follows. Existingecbc implementation promise/lane remains; source integration only after normal exact-head review. Preserve user priority: test reduction first, then declared acts/concrete Jam blockers, builder's actual self-host readiness, then Jam/full manual in parallel.","body":{"scope":"Explicit measurement amendment to ecbc722a criterion3; preserve full10x outcome and functional/test scope"}}